                    {
                        "translation_id": "c72a0128-8582-4192-bf89-64d5c1b575b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "2088c535-5034-33b6-8637-95ada45c2087",
                        "source_sense_id": "12dc26a8-80b1-301c-a8f0-cd71e5914a64",
                        "target_lang_word": "malice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "malice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8cf7024-04db-3c3a-a1b1-a02b39ae5801",
                                        "entry_id": "626ca380-dc29-391e-b118-136a6bfe5739",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intention to harm or deprive in an illegal or immoral way. Desire to take pleasure in another's misfortune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcfca1cb-cc37-40ff-979f-db4a882526dc",
                                                "sense_id": "f8cf7024-04db-3c3a-a1b1-a02b39ae5801",
                                                "text": "[…] not only was there no gratitude (which he could psychologically handle) but downright malice showed itself instead."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65b99fe4-9c98-35d6-a8b2-d6733f6e3a82",
                                        "entry_id": "626ca380-dc29-391e-b118-136a6bfe5739",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intention to do injury to another party, which in many jurisdictions is a distinguishing factor between the crimes of murder and manslaughter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "832589bd-86f9-4fe7-9be0-1e71de3753da",
                                                "sense_id": "65b99fe4-9c98-35d6-a8b2-d6733f6e3a82",
                                                "text": "The question that would have been before the jury was whether Fox committed “actual malice” in airing the claims. That required Dominion to show whether key decision makers were aware the claims were false or acted with reckless disregard for the truth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "malice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                        "entry_id": "6c5afdf9-2a23-3b99-a5d6-76d7804cac80",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To intend to cause harm; to bear malice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cc78074-4dc0-4d57-befe-3cd7908a2cb4",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "Thou blinded God (quod I) forgive me this offence, / Unwittingly I went about, to malice thy pretence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41a8b155-1b38-44cc-a587-3501197efd99",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "Who on the other ſide did ſeeme ſo farre / From malicing, or grudging his good houre, / That, all he could, he graced him with her, / Ne euer ſhewed ſigne of rancour or of iarre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35946c2c-2602-45e6-b16b-34b3a29a4070",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "His paines, his pouertie, his ſharpe aſſayes, / Through which he paſt his miſerable dayes, / Offending none, and doing good to all, / Yet being maliſt both of great and ſmall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "949a80af-142c-44f7-94ce-a708a41dbce8",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "I am so far from malicing their states, / That I begin to pity 'em."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2267964e-6ad0-463e-b2cd-9319a4b38898",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "A feeble spirited king that governed, / Who ill could guide the sceptre he did use; / His enemies, that his worth maliced, / Who both the land and him did much abuse: / The peoples love; and his apparent right, May seem sufficient motives to incite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e897286-fba3-4e14-aeb5-6ec3acd985f0",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "Here's a list of side effects / Practice tested / Covering every maliced angle / For example: / You will sleep forever / You will never sleep again"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05c3f4c2-4104-40f2-821f-7d6c521780a7",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "Robert Truswell may have been a belligerent and malicing man, a jury heard this morning during the trial of George Kieran Daunt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "213c9902-5369-4273-a3da-c96418a91857",
                                                "sense_id": "76f81848-5566-3cfe-ac62-f98115c7c274",
                                                "text": "I haven't maliced anybody, definitely not. I never used to have friends like that. I had a few who I thought were friends. Even if you have friends, things happen and friendship break up, but you move on. But I still talk to everybody."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c1242cb-eae5-4359-9d78-a745037ff81b",
                        "source_entry_id": "2088c535-5034-33b6-8637-95ada45c2087",
                        "source_sense_id": "12dc26a8-80b1-301c-a8f0-cd71e5914a64",
                        "target_lang_word": "méchanceté",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "méchanceté",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50a0a374-fd0c-398d-931d-f6a0bcac98ac",
                                        "entry_id": "6a74de49-0e57-3762-8324-5ee0f2d2e4b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Penchant à faire du mal ; mauvaiseté."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776d2523-be3f-49d5-8fba-b78d41fcad48",
                                                "sense_id": "50a0a374-fd0c-398d-931d-f6a0bcac98ac",
                                                "text": "Mais si la méchanceté et la rétivité prennent rang dans la liste des vices rédhibitoires, ce qui est fort probable, on pourra exercer non-seulement l’action en dommages-intérêts, mais encore l’action en rédhibition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1a7085b-1f7c-400f-986b-bda607ece4e0",
                                                "sense_id": "50a0a374-fd0c-398d-931d-f6a0bcac98ac",
                                                "text": "En général, l’égoïsme froid a remplacé la méchanceté active ; chacun n’envisage que lui-même et reste indifférent au malheur d’autrui."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab8e8bd8-3267-400c-86d7-e6cd848dec56",
                                                "sense_id": "50a0a374-fd0c-398d-931d-f6a0bcac98ac",
                                                "text": "Le dogme de l’incurable méchanceté de l’homme a, d'ailleurs, chez certains de ses adeptes, une autre racine : un plaisir romantique à évoquer la race humaine murée dans une misère fatale et éternelle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67cb2942-a567-4e68-88c0-8cbc1d7cea75",
                                                "sense_id": "50a0a374-fd0c-398d-931d-f6a0bcac98ac",
                                                "text": "Guindée dans son sarrau de calicot, comme une branche morte dans son écorce, presque sans nez ni lèvres, les cheveux plaqués de la même couleur pain brûlé que la peau, Mme Plinjat promène sur le monde un regard, invisible habituellement, qui semble vivre, derrière ses lunettes et ses paupières baissées, seulement quand la méchanceté l’habite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6992866-0e23-3b95-9f65-8501210146cd",
                                        "entry_id": "6a74de49-0e57-3762-8324-5ee0f2d2e4b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Opiniâtreté des enfants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43449a54-62bb-4c83-8b20-ccec41b7c93f",
                                                "sense_id": "c6992866-0e23-3b95-9f65-8501210146cd",
                                                "text": "Voyez la méchanceté de cet enfant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f36ec81b-0cc8-343e-bc05-7f2483eb4733",
                                        "entry_id": "6a74de49-0e57-3762-8324-5ee0f2d2e4b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action méchante."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91dcb533-2079-4082-bc1d-47850c89ab41",
                                                "sense_id": "f36ec81b-0cc8-343e-bc05-7f2483eb4733",
                                                "text": "Il affrontait tous les temps, bravait toutes les mers et prétendait que la mer et lui se connaissaient trop, depuis longtemps, « pour se faire des méchancetés »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5210bf-2401-4952-8d01-2bd3c3d5810e",
                                                "sense_id": "f36ec81b-0cc8-343e-bc05-7f2483eb4733",
                                                "text": "Le silence, ça n’était rien d’autre que du mépris. Et même la pire des méchancetés, la plus vile saloperie, aurait été préférable à ce mépris-là."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07e97ce-d38a-4f07-96fd-cc124db0a46c",
                                                "sense_id": "f36ec81b-0cc8-343e-bc05-7f2483eb4733",
                                                "text": "Il a fait, il a commis toute sorte de méchancetés."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87054eda-3de5-3dab-b3dd-443cb5642c59",
                                        "entry_id": "6a74de49-0e57-3762-8324-5ee0f2d2e4b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parole médisante, parole dite dans l’intention de nuire, d’offenser."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "204425a4-afab-47c5-b9ed-2a31c53b40fc",
                                                "sense_id": "87054eda-3de5-3dab-b3dd-443cb5642c59",
                                                "text": "Ce propos n’est pas une plaisanterie, c’est une méchanceté."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32233ac8-2d2e-4f1e-a1f5-c1de41c05f80",
                                                "sense_id": "87054eda-3de5-3dab-b3dd-443cb5642c59",
                                                "text": "Il n’ouvre la bouche que pour dire des méchancetés."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
